insert into public.agreement_templates (
  organization_id, template_family, template_version, status, display_title,
  rendered_content, rendered_content_type, rendered_sha256, source_sha256, notes
) values
(
  '28ad55e4-d32d-423b-80b5-481bd15dec9e',
  'venue_partner',
  '2026-09-07-counsel-review',
  'counsel_review',
  'CoastLoop Venue Partner Agreement',
  $venue$<div class="coastloop-legal-terms">
<h3>1. Appointment and purpose</h3>
<p>Venue authorizes CoastLoop to operate CoastLoop digital-signage programming only on the placements identified in the Placement Schedule. CoastLoop may use those authorized placements for Venue house content, CoastLoop house content, and third-party advertising that complies with this Agreement and CoastLoop content standards. No other display or area is authorized unless added by a written or electronically accepted amendment.</p>
<h3>2. CoastLoop services</h3>
<p>Configure and manage the CoastLoop player/software for authorized placements.</p>
<p>Schedule approved Venue house messages and third-party advertising according to the Deal Summary and platform availability.</p>
<p>Provide remote content changes, player health monitoring, and reasonable support for CoastLoop-controlled components.</p>
<p>Maintain advertiser/content review standards and respond reasonably to Venue requests concerning inappropriate or conflicting content.</p>
<h3>3. Venue responsibilities</h3>
<p>Provide reasonable access to the authorized displays and any agreed power/network connection needed for installation, maintenance, and removal.</p>
<p>Maintain Venue-owned televisions, power, and internet service unless the Deal Summary assigns a different responsibility.</p>
<p>Not intentionally disable, remove, alter, resell, or interfere with CoastLoop-controlled hardware/software without notice, except for safety, emergency, or normal Venue operations.</p>
<p>Provide house content and brand assets it wants displayed and confirm that Venue has the rights necessary for CoastLoop to use them.</p>
<h3>4. Placement modes and sports / broadcast screens</h3>
<p>Each authorized screen is assigned an operating mode in the Placement Schedule. CoastLoop does not receive rights to alter, interrupt, overlay, or replace programming on any non-authorized display. If a screen is designated “Scheduled CoastLoop,” the parties will follow the agreed schedule or switching method. Any automatic replacement of third-party broadcast commercials requires separate technical and legal approval and is not granted by this Agreement.</p>
<h3>5. Advertising inventory and Venue house content</h3>
<p>Venue receives the house-content allocation shown in the Deal Summary. CoastLoop may sell and schedule the remaining CoastLoop inventory on authorized placements, subject to agreed category exclusions and reasonable content standards. CoastLoop controls campaign trafficking, sequencing, and scheduling unless a specific placement or frequency guarantee is written into the Deal Summary or an amendment.</p>
<h3>6. Content standards and takedown</h3>
<p>CoastLoop may reject, suspend, or remove content that is unlawful, deceptive, infringing, obscene, unsafe, technically defective, or reasonably likely to create material reputational harm. Venue may identify reasonable category exclusions in the Deal Summary and may request prompt removal of a specific ad for a legitimate brand-safety concern. Unless Venue expressly opts in, political campaign advertising is excluded from Venue placements.</p>
<h3>7. Compensation, taxes, and payment setup</h3>
<p>Any cash host compensation is only the amount and schedule shown in the Deal Summary. If compensation is “None,” Venue’s consideration may include CoastLoop signage management, house-content inventory, and other agreed services. Venue will provide tax/payment information reasonably required for lawful payment processing after execution of this Agreement. Each party is responsible for its own taxes except as required by law.</p>
<h3>8. Equipment and property</h3>
<p>Venue retains ownership of its existing televisions and fixtures. CoastLoop retains ownership of CoastLoop-provided hardware unless the Deal Summary states otherwise. CoastLoop will use reasonable care while installing or servicing equipment. At termination, CoastLoop may remove its equipment and restore the immediate installation area in a commercially reasonable manner, ordinary wear and pre-existing conditions excepted.</p>
<h3>9. Public listing, trademarks, and photographs</h3>
<p>If Public Venue Listing is marked “Yes,” Venue grants CoastLoop a limited, non-exclusive, revocable license during the Term to use Venue’s approved name and logo solely to identify Venue as a CoastLoop placement/partner and market available advertising inventory. If Approved Venue Photography is marked “Yes,” CoastLoop may use approved photographs of the authorized placement for sales, previews, case studies, and network marketing. No endorsement beyond the approved relationship may be implied. If either election is “No,” CoastLoop may still use Venue information internally to operate the service.</p>
<h3>10. Telemetry, privacy, and audience measurement</h3>
<p>CoastLoop may collect ordinary device and playback telemetry such as player status, uptime, scheduling events, error logs, and ad-play events. This base Agreement does NOT authorize camera-based or sensor-based audience measurement, facial recognition, biometric identification, persistent person tracking, or storage of customer video for advertising analytics. Any future camera/sensor audience measurement requires a separate written addendum accepted by Venue before activation.</p>
<h3>11. Term; suspension; termination</h3>
<p>The Term is shown in the Deal Summary. Either party may suspend an affected placement immediately for safety, legal compliance, material technical risk, or material content-policy concern. Unless the Deal Summary states a different pilot/termination rule, either party may terminate for material breach that remains uncured for ten (10) days after written notice, or immediately for unlawful use, intentional tampering, or conduct creating substantial safety or legal risk. The parties may also agree electronically to an earlier removal date.</p>
<h3>12. Warranties; liability; indemnity</h3>
<p>Each party represents that it has authority to enter this Agreement and grant the rights it grants. CoastLoop will perform its services in a commercially reasonable manner but does not guarantee specific foot traffic, views, leads, sales, or uninterrupted operation. To the maximum extent permitted by law, neither party is liable to the other for consequential, special, exemplary, or lost-profit damages arising from this Agreement. Each party will defend and indemnify the other from third-party claims to the extent caused by its own unlawful content, infringement, gross negligence, or willful misconduct. Any additional insurance requirement must be stated in the Deal Summary or an amendment.</p>
<h3>13. Independent businesses; no exclusivity</h3>
<p>The parties are independent contractors. This Agreement does not create a partnership, franchise, employment relationship, fiduciary relationship, or exclusivity unless the Deal Summary expressly states otherwise.</p>
<h3>14. Notices and electronic transactions</h3>
<p>The parties agree to conduct this transaction electronically. Notices may be sent to the email/mobile contacts in the Deal Summary, except that a party may provide an updated notice contact. Electronic signatures and electronic records are intended to have the same effect as originals. CoastLoop will provide the signer access to a retainable copy of the executed Agreement. Amendments may be accepted electronically if the changed terms are presented to and accepted by authorized representatives.</p>
<h3>15. Governing law; entire agreement</h3>
<p>South Carolina law governs this Agreement without regard to conflicts-of-law rules. Any action relating to this Agreement will be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Horry County, South Carolina, unless the parties agree otherwise in writing. The Deal Summary, Placement Schedule, this Agreement, and any signed amendments are the entire agreement concerning the authorized CoastLoop placements and supersede prior discussions on that subject. If there is a conflict, the most specific deal-specific term controls over general boilerplate.</p>
</div>$venue$,
  'text/html',
  '8ea894d9104adcb6f4f4f8fd59067ef52b78505e5db2eace82cca7f4fa9259e3',
  'ff4fe1df60db623d635a8ceb1bf5eb547f28e6a87f6c6ebb5bfa68ddb24468f7',
  'COUNSEL REVIEW ONLY. Source DOCX still contains [COASTLOOP LEGAL ENTITY NAME]. Do not lock or sign until contracting entity is completed and South Carolina counsel approves.'
),
(
  '28ad55e4-d32d-423b-80b5-481bd15dec9e',
  'advertising_order_terms',
  '2026-09-07-counsel-review',
  'counsel_review',
  'CoastLoop Advertising Order + Terms',
  $advertiser$<div class="coastloop-legal-terms">
<h3>1. Order and campaign delivery</h3>
<p>Advertiser purchases the advertising package described in the Order Summary. CoastLoop will use commercially reasonable efforts to deliver the campaign according to the stated market/placement scope, term, creative length, and frequency rules. Unless the Order guarantees a named screen or fixed position, CoastLoop may rotate or substitute comparable authorized placements within the purchased scope to operate the network efficiently.</p>
<h3>2. Measurement definitions and forecasts</h3>
<p>Verified Play: a CoastLoop-defined playback event confirmed by player/platform telemetry under the reporting methodology in effect for the campaign.</p>
<p>Projected Plays: a forecast based on screen count, schedule, loop length, package frequency, and expected uptime; projected figures are not guaranteed actual plays.</p>
<p>Estimated Audience / Opportunities to See: an estimate only when CoastLoop discloses the methodology. Estimated traffic is not the same as a verified human view.</p>
<p>CoastLoop does not guarantee impressions, attention, leads, sales, conversions, or return on ad spend unless a specific written guarantee appears in the Order Summary.</p>
<h3>3. Creative rights and authorization</h3>
<p>Advertiser represents that it owns or has permission to use all logos, images, trademarks, music, claims, offers, testimonials, and other materials it supplies or directs CoastLoop to use. Advertiser grants CoastLoop a limited license during the campaign to reproduce, crop, resize, animate, format, adapt, and display those materials solely to create, deliver, promote, and report on the campaign. If Advertiser selects “Use my website,” Advertiser authorizes CoastLoop to use brand assets and content from domains/pages controlled by Advertiser for campaign creation, subject to Advertiser’s rights representation.</p>
<h3>4. CoastLoop-created / AI-assisted creative</h3>
<p>If Advertiser asks CoastLoop to make the ad, CoastLoop may use human, automated, and AI-assisted creative tools. Advertiser remains responsible for the truthfulness and legal sufficiency of its business claims, offers, prices, endorsements, and regulated statements. Unless Advertiser explicitly authorizes automatic approval, CoastLoop-created creative will not go live until Advertiser approves the final version electronically.</p>
<h3>5. Content standards</h3>
<p>CoastLoop may reject, require changes to, pause, or remove creative that is unlawful, deceptive, defamatory, infringing, obscene, technically defective, inconsistent with venue restrictions, or reasonably likely to create material safety or reputational risk. Advertiser will promptly provide substantiation for objective claims if reasonably requested. Venue-specific category exclusions may limit delivery to particular placements.</p>
<h3>6. Payment, activation, cancellation, and make-goods</h3>
<p>Payment terms are shown in the Order Summary. Unless otherwise stated, prepaid campaigns are scheduled after payment and creative approval. If Advertiser cancels before activation, CoastLoop will refund prepaid media charges less any separately disclosed non-recoverable creative/setup cost. After activation, prepaid amounts are non-refundable except for material undelivered service caused by CoastLoop; in that situation CoastLoop may provide comparable make-good delivery, account credit, or a prorated refund for the materially undelivered portion. Temporary screen outages, venue closures, force majeure, or network maintenance may cause scheduling changes and are addressed through reasonable make-goods when commercially feasible.</p>
<h3>7. Campaign changes</h3>
<p>Advertiser may request reasonable creative or offer changes through the campaign portal. Changes that alter package scope, term, frequency, market, or price require an updated Order Summary or electronically accepted amendment. CoastLoop may pause delivery while materially changed creative is reviewed.</p>
<h3>8. Reporting and data</h3>
<p>CoastLoop may provide campaign reporting that includes delivery, placement, uptime, and other available metrics. Reports may contain estimates and modeled values, which will be labeled accordingly. Historical campaign and order records may be retained for accounting, compliance, dispute resolution, and performance reporting.</p>
<h3>9. Privacy and future audience measurement</h3>
<p>This Order does not promise camera-based audience measurement. If CoastLoop later offers privacy-preserving aggregate audience measurement at participating venues, any metric shown to Advertiser will be described according to its methodology and applicable venue authorization. CoastLoop does not represent that current playback telemetry identifies individual viewers.</p>
<h3>10. Advertiser warranties and indemnity</h3>
<p>Advertiser represents that it has authority to enter this Order and that its creative, offers, claims, products, and services comply with applicable law and do not infringe third-party rights. Advertiser will defend and indemnify CoastLoop and participating venues from third-party claims arising from Advertiser-provided content, claims, products/services, infringement, or unlawful instructions, except to the extent caused by CoastLoop’s own gross negligence or willful misconduct.</p>
<h3>11. CoastLoop warranty and limitation of liability</h3>
<p>CoastLoop will perform the advertising service in a commercially reasonable manner. Except for express promises in the Order Summary, the service is provided without guarantees of business outcome. To the maximum extent permitted by law, CoastLoop and participating venues will not be liable for consequential, special, exemplary, punitive, or lost-profit damages arising from this Order. CoastLoop’s aggregate liability for a campaign will not exceed the amount actually paid to CoastLoop for that campaign, except where applicable law does not permit that limitation.</p>
<h3>12. Electronic acceptance; governing law</h3>
<p>The parties agree to conduct this transaction electronically. Electronic signatures and records are intended to have the same effect as originals, and CoastLoop will provide access to a retainable executed copy. South Carolina law governs this Order. Any action relating to it will be brought in a court of competent jurisdiction in Horry County, South Carolina, unless the parties agree otherwise in writing. The Order Summary and these Terms, together with any electronically accepted amendment, are the entire agreement for this campaign.</p>
</div>$advertiser$,
  'text/html',
  '5eab32e6906f7b745da60f668b6beae545c1bb6c4955d04a682260923d2d1b23',
